        "authorName": "NULL JSFX",
        "name": {
          "en-US": "Remote for Mixers"
        },
        "summary": {
          "en-US": "Beta: your digital mixer on your phone or tablet. Faders, mutes, sends, meters."
        },
        "description": {
          "en-US": "Remote for Mixers controls a digital mixer from your Android phone or tablet over the mixer's Wi-Fi or your local network. It works with Behringer X AIR mixers (XR12, XR16, XR18, X18) with the Behringer X32 and Midas M32 families (X32, Compact, Producer, Rack, Core; M32, M32R, M32C) with the Behringer WING (WING, Compact, Rack; no meters yet) with the Allen & Heath SQ (SQ-5, SQ-6, SQ-7: faders, mutes, pan, sends and mute groups; its protocol has no names, meters or solo) with the Allen & Heath Qu (Qu-16, Qu-24, Qu-32, Qu-Pac, Qu-SB: names, faders, mutes, pan, mix sends, mute groups and meters) with the Allen & Heath CQ (CQ-12T, CQ-18T, CQ-20B: faders, mutes, pan, sends to the outputs, DCAs and mute groups; its protocol has no names or meters) with the Allen & Heath dLive and Avantis (names, colours, faders, mutes, sends to the aux mixes, DCAs and mute groups; their protocol has no pan or meters) and, in beta, with the Yamaha CL, QL, TF and DM7 (CL5, CL3, CL1, QL5, QL1, TF5, TF3, TF1, TF-RACK, DM7, DM7 Compact: names, colours, faders, on/off, pan, mix sends, DCAs and mute groups; no meters yet).\n\nThis is a beta: it is tested against software X AIR, X32, WING, SQ, Qu, CQ, dLive, Avantis and Yamaha consoles. Please report anything that behaves differently on your mixer.\n\n<b>What it does</b>\n<ul>\n<li>Finds the mixer on the network and recognises its model by itself, with step-by-step connection help. You can also type its IP address.</li>\n<li>Channels, aux, FX returns, buses, FX sends, DCAs and the main mix: faders, mute, solo, pan and meters, with names and colours from the mixer.</li>\n<li>Sends on faders: pick a bus or FX and the faders become the sends to it, for monitor mixes.</li>\n<li>Mute groups and Clear solo.</li>\n<li>My mix: lock a musician's phone to the sends of their own monitor bus, without mute or solo.</li>\n<li>Screen lock that opens only with a long press, so a stray touch on stage changes nothing.</li>\n<li>Faders move with your finger from where they are; they never jump to where you touch.</li>\n</ul>\n\nPart of NULL JSFX (https://nulljsfx.tech): free, MIT licensed, no ads, no tracking, no account. Privacy: https://nulljsfx.tech/privacy/ X AIR, X32, M32, WING, Allen & Heath, SQ and Qu are trademarks of their owners. This app is independent and is not made or endorsed by them.\n"
        },
